          "entries": [
            { "id": 1, "type": "user", "message": "Where does an offer’s rate come from, and what would a rate-history chart on the offer page touch?", "lookingAt": "Offer · Typical" },
            { "id": 2, "type": "tool", "name": "Grep", "summary": "rate in prelude/borrower-architecture" },
            {
              "id": 3,
              "type": "text",
              "pieces": [
                { "kind": "text", "html": "<p>Rates come from the lender, and are kept with the offer:</p>" },
                {
                  "kind": "unread",
                  "tag": "prelude-flow-1",
                  "code": "# Where a rate comes from\n1. lender-api: Sends the offer with its rate\n2. offers-api: Validates it\n3. rates: Stores it beside the offer",
                  "why": "<code>offers-api</code> and <code>rates</code> aren’t parts in borrower-portal’s architecture."
                },
                { "kind": "text", "html": "<p>A rate-history chart would need these:</p>" },
                {
                  "kind": "unread",
                  "tag": "prelude-map-1",
                  "code": "offer-pages, pricing\noffer-store: keeps each rate it was sent",
                  "why": "line 1, <code>offer-pages, pricing</code>, isn’t one part. A map takes one part per line, each with an optional “: ” and a note."
                },
                { "kind": "text", "html": "<p>And roughly how the last six months would look for Northfield’s offer:</p>" },
                {
                  "kind": "unread",
                  "tag": "prelude-chart-1",
                  "code": "May 6.1\nJun 6.0\nJul 5.8\nAug 5.9\nSep 5.7\nOct 5.6",
                  "why": "Prelude doesn’t know <code>prelude-chart-1</code>. It draws <code>prelude-flow-1</code> and <code>prelude-map-1</code>."
                },
                { "kind": "text", "html": "<p>The offer store only keeps the latest rate today, so the history would have to start being kept before the chart has anything to show.</p>" }
              ]
            },
